yaml/string/double-quoted
description: Escapable string between double quotes
- >
  The double-quoted style is the escapable one - the only style that can spell ANY character -
  and a SUPERCLASS of
  [json/string](::language:concretes:07-json_code:01-json_scalar:00-json_string): every
  JSON string is a valid double-quoted scalar, and YAML adds more escapes (`\0`, `\e`, `\xXX`,
  `\UXXXXXXXX` and kin over JSON's set), tolerates a literal tab, and FOLDS - the scalar may
  span lines, single breaks becoming spaces:
- !!<format: text/x-yaml> |
  a: "line one\nline \"two\"\tand a tab"
  b: "these two lines
    become one"
- *..:..:..:..:..:07-json_code:01-json_scalar:00-json_string
